WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.970
The official Dark Souls' Design Works books
are incredible, with interviews and concept

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.720
art that give wonderful insight into the development
process.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.890
But the thing I want to talk to you about
today, isn't in the Dark Souls design works.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:19.040
Specifically, it was left out.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.000
Archived on Resetera, are these fantastic
images, allegedly drawn by an artist named

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.330
Jocus Wang.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:30.500
There's a dark hellscape, where your eyes
are drawn towards a bleeding sun..There's

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.499
art that looks like it might have inspired
Cainhurst library, from Bloodborne..There's

00:00:35.499 --> 00:00:41.489
a gothic courtyard..that one commenter points
out merges the Berlin Cathedral, and the Louvre..there

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:46.679
are statues that might once have been graceful,
but have become horrifically worn..There's

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:50.300
concept art of Archdragon Peak.. a tired settlement,
and my personal favourite, a sort of abandoned

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:56.909
sewer area, with just enough light filtering
through to nourish gentle growths of moss.

00:00:56.909 --> 00:01:02.569
I love the verticality here..and the way the
artist uses light to draw you into every little

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:03.859
nook..it's masterful.

00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:09.590
Now, that first image should be familiar to
anyone who saw the Dark Souls 3 leaks published

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.920
all the way back in 2015.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:17.950
This famous screenshot showed that same bleeding
sun, and a world reduced to a hellish ruin.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:24.270
I remember, those leaks were especially shitty
for From Software back then, because they

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:30.909
were clearly outdated and misleading..but
looking back now, along with the artwork,

00:01:30.909 --> 00:01:37.340
these feel more like lost treasures to me
- and they do wonders for the intrigue behind

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.340
these games.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.350
I'll of course take this down if From Soft
or Jocus request it, but we get precious little

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:48.390
insight into the development process, and
it's fun to imagine the game that could have

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.390
been.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.490
Of course, if you want some official insight
into these games, go and buy the official

00:01:57.606 --> 00:02:03.446
It's no secret that when you kill Ornstein
first in Dark Souls 1, Smough grows larger.

00:02:03.446 --> 00:02:06.636
And when you kill Smough first, Ornstein grows
larger.

00:02:06.636 --> 00:02:07.916
Or..does he?

00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:14.416
Recently, Zullie revealed a clever camera
trick in this scene - whereby Ornstein actually

00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:20.046
stays the same size, while Smough's body,
and the arena, shrinks instead.

00:02:20.046 --> 00:02:24.786
Considering there isn't a functional size
scaling value for character models in this

00:02:24.786 --> 00:02:30.676
game, Zullie speculates that this would have
been far easier for them to implement.

00:02:30.676 --> 00:02:35.616
These Secrets videos have become, first and
foremost, a way to point you towards other

00:02:35.616 --> 00:02:41.776
creators and creations that can enrich your
appreciation of the Souls series..so please,

00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:42.776
go and click all the links in the description,
before you leave.

00:02:42.776 --> 00:02:45.586
And lately, Zullie the Witch has been absolutely
killing it.

00:02:45.586 --> 00:02:51.756
The algorithm has finally taken a liking to
her short, entertaining videos..and I feel

00:02:51.756 --> 00:02:54.446
like it all started with this one.

00:02:54.446 --> 00:02:57.726
As you know, if you kill Ornstein first, you
get super smough.

00:02:57.726 --> 00:03:00.146
If you kill smough first, you get super ornstein.

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.146
But..

00:03:01.146 --> 00:03:05.866
"What happens if you kill Ornstein and Smough
at the same time"?

00:03:05.866 --> 00:03:10.066
By using an AOE attack to force a tie..the
winner is..Smough.

00:03:10.066 --> 00:03:18.206
That's because the event is tied to whichever
animation ends first, and Smough has a faster

00:03:18.206 --> 00:03:19.256
death animation.

00:03:19.256 --> 00:03:24.826
But what happens if you kill Ornstein first,
then Smough quickly after, to line up their

00:03:24.826 --> 00:03:25.826
animations?

00:03:25.826 --> 00:03:27.266
Well..you can't.

00:03:27.266 --> 00:03:31.496
From Software thought of this, and added immortality
to the other character once their partner

00:03:31.496 --> 00:03:32.496
dies.

00:03:32.496 --> 00:03:38.546
Interestingly, if animation length is removed
as a factor, and both their HP are set to

00:03:38.546 --> 00:03:45.556
0..then there is code that enables Ornstein
as the winner, every time.

00:03:45.556 --> 00:03:50.506
Luckily, this isn't possible in regular gameplay..because
it also softlocks the fight.

00:03:50.506 --> 00:03:55.146
Another thing I found fascinating is how they
workaround boss health bar issues in some

00:03:55.146 --> 00:03:56.146
fights.

00:03:56.146 --> 00:04:02.176
In fights like the four kings, or the deacons,
there's actually another member hidden off-screen.

00:04:02.176 --> 00:04:06.596
It's their health bar you see at the bottom
of your screen, and they take damage on behalf

00:04:06.596 --> 00:04:08.956
of all the other members you hit.

00:04:08.956 --> 00:04:13.936
This also goes for the Gael boss fight, where
second phase Gael waits in this structure

00:04:13.936 --> 00:04:15.156
in the distance.

00:04:15.156 --> 00:04:20.176
When phase two starts, during the cutscene,
this damaged second phase teleports down,

00:04:20.176 --> 00:04:22.036
and the fight continues.

00:04:22.036 --> 00:04:26.436
From Software tend to remove a lot of cut
content from their games these days, but this

00:04:26.436 --> 00:04:30.316
wolf snuck through on a PS4 patch for Dark
Souls 3.

00:04:30.316 --> 00:04:37.836
It bears resemblance to the Old Wolf of Farron
covenant model, down to the same little bronze

00:04:37.836 --> 00:04:38.836
bracelet.

00:04:38.836 --> 00:04:43.706
Once, it seems, this was planned to be a part
of the Abyss Watchers boss fight.

00:04:43.706 --> 00:04:50.806
Here, in a cutscene found by micb123 and uploaded
by Dropoff, we see the wolf appear as a part

00:04:50.806 --> 00:04:52.566
of the phase 2 revival cutscene.

00:04:52.566 --> 00:05:00.336
Here's a hot take: but I'm not sure I want
another wolf fight in the Souls series!

00:05:00.336 --> 00:05:01.346
So I'm..pretty glad this was changed.

00:05:01.346 --> 00:05:06.486
We've talked before about how there are grabs
you can escape in Dark Souls 1 by pressing

00:05:06.486 --> 00:05:11.626
R1 and L1, but for many years, such a thing
was rumoured to be a glitch.

00:05:11.626 --> 00:05:14.396
Turns out, it has its own dedicated system.

00:05:14.396 --> 00:05:19.536
In this video, Zullie showcases how grabs
technically have their own hp.

00:05:19.536 --> 00:05:26.416
Each escapable grab has 25hp, and each press
of R1 or L1 reduces the hp by 1.

00:05:26.416 --> 00:05:30.076
Get it to 0, and your character performs the
escape throw animation.

00:05:30.076 --> 00:05:35.336
Having the hp of the grab makes your button
mashing feel so much more meaningful, and

00:05:35.336 --> 00:05:44.256
I'm kind of surprised they didn't add a sort
of status meter for it, in-game.

00:05:44.256 --> 00:05:49.296
In a recent Demon's Souls Prepare to Cry,
we talked about Boletaria's proclivity for

00:05:49.296 --> 00:05:54.596
slaves, and how important they were to their
wars, and greater society.

00:05:54.596 --> 00:05:58.786
Turns out, slaves are more entrenched in the
game than I thought.

00:05:58.786 --> 00:06:02.726
As you head up to fight Allant, the final
boss, take a look through the walls of the

00:06:02.726 --> 00:06:03.846
elevator.

00:06:03.846 --> 00:06:09.385
Hidden within the mechanism, are two slave
soldiers, working tirelessly to bring visitors

00:06:09.385 --> 00:06:10.956
up to their master.

00:06:10.956 --> 00:06:16.316
Moving into Demon's Souls - everyone knows
that the manta rays detach from the storm

00:06:16.316 --> 00:06:20.369
king to start attacking you..but did you know
that the projectiles they shoot are..also,

00:06:20.369 --> 00:06:21.369
actually smaller rays?

00:06:21.369 --> 00:06:22.369
In the remake, they are, at least.

00:06:22.369 --> 00:06:24.086
In the original, they were simple javelins.

00:06:24.086 --> 00:06:28.956
I guess Bluepoint wanted to give you another
excuse to use their photo mode.

00:06:28.956 --> 00:06:34.246
Recently, a fantastic article was posted to
the Playstation blog, detailing the process

00:06:34.246 --> 00:06:43.846
behind capturing the incredible animations
of the Demon's Souls remake.

00:06:43.846 --> 00:06:57.746
While the cadence of animations and movement
hasn't changed, the animations themselves

00:06:57.746 --> 00:07:01.096
are updated..every single one of them.

00:07:01.096 --> 00:07:05.896
"Performed too quickly, the movements would
lack clear arcs and silhouettes.

00:07:05.896 --> 00:07:16.266
Performed too slowly, they might lose their
weight and inertia".

00:07:16.266 --> 00:07:20.385
The article is a great read, explaining how
and why this project was difficult, even for

00:07:20.385 --> 00:07:25.195
someone with 20 years of mo cap experience.

00:07:25.195 --> 00:07:30.766
Most striking in the Remake are the brutal,
complex ripostes and backstabs - all of which

00:07:30.766 --> 00:07:35.706
have different animations depending on the
weapon you use, and how many hands you carry

00:07:35.706 --> 00:07:36.866
it with.

00:07:36.866 --> 00:07:41.756
This game is a technical marvel, and a part
of me wishes From Software had a bit of that

00:07:41.756 --> 00:07:43.576
Bluepoint polish in them.

00:07:43.576 --> 00:07:48.986
Don't get me wrong, From Software's current
game development cycle IS super efficient

00:07:48.986 --> 00:07:55.626
and they pump out quality games way faster
than most studios, but with Elden Ring looking

00:07:55.626 --> 00:08:02.056
a lot like Dark Souls 3, their game appearance
IS starting to age a little, and I wonder

00:08:02.056 --> 00:08:05.146
when we might see a visual leap forward from
them.

00:08:05.146 --> 00:08:10.385
I'm not saying it has to happen now, but sooner
or later, something is going to give.

00:08:10.385 --> 00:08:15.266
Moving on to Sekiro - we've talked about the
Gyoubu skip before, and even the Blazing bull

00:08:15.266 --> 00:08:16.845
skip after that.

00:08:16.845 --> 00:08:21.096
But what if you perform these glitches during
the Gauntlets of Strength?

00:08:21.096 --> 00:08:25.266
One twitter user did just that (@full_metalmoron)
and shared it with me, revealing a world that

00:08:25.266 --> 00:08:27.456
renders in in a strange way.

00:08:27.456 --> 00:08:30.425
You should try it, and see what oddities you
can find.

00:08:30.425 --> 00:08:36.766
The best place to visit, by far, is the silvergrass
field, which shows a lightning storm during

00:08:36.766 --> 00:08:40.235
day, with surreal reflections and lighting.

00:08:40.235 --> 00:08:46.805
You've all seen..or heard, the Sentries in
Sekiro..who hammer a metal pan with a metal

00:08:46.805 --> 00:08:47.805
rod.

00:08:47.805 --> 00:08:54.956
But did you know..they can actually attack
you?

00:08:54.956 --> 00:08:59.386
Stand in melee range, and parry them four
times, and you'll be able to perform a fairly

00:08:59.386 --> 00:09:02.115
unique riposte to kill them.

00:09:02.115 --> 00:09:08.605
I learned about this from Ongbal, a Sekiro
master who uploads stunning clips of him flawlessly

00:09:08.605 --> 00:09:10.576
killing bosses in this game.

00:09:10.576 --> 00:09:15.936
Not only are there no errors in his clips,
but he weaves interesting combos into his

00:09:15.936 --> 00:09:19.225
fights whenever possible, leading to some
incredibly quick takedowns.

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:25.785
For someone like me, who adores Sekiro's combat,
they're well worth a sub.

00:09:25.785 --> 00:09:30.475
Now..Sekiro's combat is good and all..but
this..THIS is gameplay.

00:09:30.475 --> 00:09:31.475
Poison rolling.

00:09:31.475 --> 00:09:36.115
Researched by Limit Breakers a few months
ago, we learned that the Hunter's roll inherits

00:09:36.115 --> 00:09:40.835
the effects of poison gems attached to the
right hand weapon.

00:09:40.835 --> 00:09:47.465
This comes in two flavours - slow poison,
which builds up then drains hp over time,

00:09:47.465 --> 00:09:51.526
and rapid poison, which builds up and deals
damage all at once.

00:09:51.526 --> 00:09:56.465
Relative to slow, rapid is a way better option..and
can even be used against some bosses with

00:09:56.465 --> 00:09:59.715
big HP pools, to good effect.

00:09:59.715 --> 00:10:07.876
But relative to actually..you know, hitting
enemies..or actually using good gems..no.

00:10:07.876 --> 00:10:09.995
Rolling poison isn't that great.

00:10:09.995 --> 00:10:14.766
You can use the hunter's bone to speed up
the process, but many bosses have 999 poison

00:10:14.766 --> 00:10:16.925
resistance anyway, making it a pointless endeavor.

00:10:16.925 --> 00:10:24.085
The one thing it is good for is entertaining
challenge runs..so make sure you check out

00:10:24.085 --> 00:10:25.085
YMFAH's "pacifist run".

00:10:25.085 --> 00:10:29.415
You'll learn a ton more secrets from him in
that one (gascoigne disappear)

00:10:29.415 --> 00:10:34.586
Limit Breakers put out another video recently
showing off the "Bow Bash" of Demon's Souls,

00:10:34.586 --> 00:10:37.576
something that hasn't really been showcased
on YouTube before.

00:10:37.576 --> 00:10:42.356
It has a strange input, requiring you to face
away from your opponent before snapping in

00:10:42.356 --> 00:10:45.196
the opposite direction, and pressing R2.

00:10:45.196 --> 00:10:50.335
Damage is modified by which bow you use, and
how upgraded it is..but I'll leave it to Limit

00:10:50.335 --> 00:10:52.216
to teach you the specifics.

00:10:52.216 --> 00:10:56.636
One of the best things about the Remake is
that all of this jank was left in this super

00:10:56.636 --> 00:10:59.365
modern ps5 title.

00:10:59.365 --> 00:11:05.275
There were some things in this game I never
thought we'd see..and Vicar Amelia's face

00:11:05.275 --> 00:11:07.896
before she transforms, was one of them.

00:11:07.896 --> 00:11:15.436
Her side profile definitely gives a younger,
and prettier impression to my imagination..than

00:11:15.436 --> 00:11:17.025
the reality.

00:11:17.025 --> 00:11:23.016
Luckily, Bloodborne has been explored a ton
in recent years thanks to new tools and talented

00:11:23.016 --> 00:11:28.675
modders like LanceMcDonald..though perhaps
some things are better left unseen.

00:11:28.675 --> 00:11:34.186
Lance also has a video showing off a never-before-seen
cutscene from the Wet Nurse boss, so go and

00:11:34.186 --> 00:11:35.876
check out his channel for that.

00:11:35.876 --> 00:11:42.166
Last, with a fantastic video idea, is Illusorywall,
who got AI to generate a real-life cast of

00:11:42.166 --> 00:11:44.766
Dark Souls, based on their in-game models.

00:11:44.766 --> 00:11:50.915
Some of this stuff is absolutely stunning..some
is horrifying..but all of it almost makes

00:11:50.915 --> 00:11:53.775
me want a film based on these games.

00:11:53.775 --> 00:11:58.907
I mean..it'd be a nightmare trying to write
a movie script for the Souls series, but as

00:11:58.907 --> 00:12:03.555
IllusoryWall notes in the video, a lot of
these faces already bear resemblance to real-life

00:12:03.555 --> 00:12:04.706
actors.

00:12:04.706 --> 00:12:09.036
Here's one last crazy secret..your middle
mouse button can be used to open links in

00:12:09.036 --> 00:12:13.855
new tabs, and that's exactly what you should
do for every link in the description.

00:12:13.855 --> 00:12:15.706
Including Soul Arts!

00:12:15.706 --> 00:12:21.415
The campaign is literally about to end, so
become a backer, if you want to join us on

00:12:21.415 --> 00:12:24.245
this journey to produce something really special.

00:12:24.245 --> 00:12:25.455
Thank you for watching.

00:12:25.455 --> 00:12:26.529
Hopefully we get some Elden Ring news soon.

00:12:26.529 --> 00:12:26.545
I'll see you in the next one.

